    "execution_order": "Algorithms are interleaved by repetition with a deterministic case-specific rotation.",
    "summary_statistic": "Median over successful repetitions; Q1, Q3, IQR, min, max, mean, and sample standard deviation are retained.",
    "correctness_rule": "Every expected algorithm in a semantic group must finish every repetition, produce a stable count, and agree with the other algorithms in that group.",
    "cardinality_boundary": "original_cardinality follows the 2022 TD-Tree paper and is reported separately; its counts and timings are not used as a consecutive-semantics speedup denominator.",
    "prefiltered_boundary": "Full stackoverflow and bitcoin raw inputs remain outside the bounded matching matrix on this 24 GiB WSL host. Their supplied filtered graphs and deterministic edge-history-preserving 5% samples are used instead.",
    "gpu_boundary": "ROCm 7.2.4 detects the Radeon 8060S (gfx1151) through WSL /dev/dxg and a real transfer-kernel-transfer verification passed. The GPU prototype is a fused device-resident Candidate-DAG frontier executor without CPU runtime memo tables; it is compared with both CPU no-memo 1T and full CPU Gopher.",
    "single_thread_boundary": "Original and ours are serial implementations and are recorded with threads=1. CPU Gopher single-thread comparisons use --threads 1 and numerical-runtime thread caps.",
    "provenance": "The runner records SHA-256 for each executable, dataset, query, and used manifest."
  },
